    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103246" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσᾰράριος</span></b> , also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσαραλ-</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσαλαρ-</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσσαλαρ-</span></b> , etc., ὁ, = Lat.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tesserarius,
				non-commissioned officer who communicates the password</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				43r
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				ii 21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, etc.; also a civil official of uncertain
			functions, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				10.1106.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>, <i>I Got.</i><i><span class="en">
				6.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. πλοῖα</span>
			<i>dispatch</i>-boats, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).941
			</span></i> (Tenos, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>).</div>
